        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be possible on the latest `main`.\n\nUnfortunately, it required a slightly breaking change to implement cleanly. Now using `''` or `{}` as a reference text will [set truly empty reference text](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/8bf5c57bc82dd590932faa41bfde9fd6d40a9433/doc/mini-diff.txt#L520-L529) and not set single line or unset it completely respectively. The `MiniDiff.set_ref_text(buf_id)` (i.e. using default argument for reference text) still unsets the text.\n\nThanks again for noticing this issue and suggesting the improvement!",
